* Functional LMC555 approximation for low-frequency logic/timing simulation.
* Datasheet: https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/lmc555.pdf
* Not a TI manufacturer model; not validated for device limits or tolerances.
* Same terminal order as the user's original model. All references use GND.
* Finite transition time and a hysteretic switch replace the algebraic latch.
* Does not model supply current, accurate output drive, or power dissipation.
.SUBCKT LMC555 GND TRIG OUT RESET CONT THRES DISCH VDD
R_TOP VDD CONT 100k
R_MID CONT REF 100k
R_BOT REF GND 100k

* CMD +1: reset latch; -1: set latch; 0: retain hysteretic switch state.
* TI datasheet section 7.4.1: RESET overrides TRIG; TRIG overrides THRES.
* Supply below the specified 1.5 V operating minimum is forced inactive.
B_CMD CMD GND V={if(V(VDD,GND)<1.5,1,if(V(RESET,GND)<0.75,1,if(V(TRIG,GND)<V(REF,GND),-1,if(V(THRES,GND)>V(CONT,GND),1,0))))}
V_LOGIC ONE GND 1
R_LATCH ONE RAW 1k
S_LATCH RAW GND CMD GND SW_LATCH ON
.MODEL SW_LATCH SW(RON=1 ROFF=1e12 VT=0 VH=0.5)

* Approximate 1 us propagation/edge smoothing; not a datasheet timing fit.
R_DELAY RAW STATE 1k
C_DELAY STATE GND 1n IC=0
B_DRIVE DRIVE GND V={max(V(VDD,GND),0)*0.5*(1+tanh((V(STATE,GND)-0.5)/0.05))}
R_OUT DRIVE OUT 10

* Correct phase: OUT low -> discharge ON; OUT high -> discharge OFF.
S_DISCH DISCH GND GND STATE SW_DISCH ON
.MODEL SW_DISCH SW(RON=10 ROFF=1e12 VT=-0.5 VH=0.05)
.ENDS LMC555
